d 'ATIP_MAHAL': module for genuine multivariate outlier detection via Mahalanobis distance 
d
d  atip_mahal computes the multivariate Mahalanobis distance (2+
d variables) within groups, detecting anomalous combinations that
d no univariate rule can see. By default it uses the Minimum
d Covariance Determinant estimator (Rousseeuw and Van Driessen
d 1999, Technometrics 41:212-223) instead of the classical
d covariance, which is highly robust to masking -- validated by
d simulation (1,000 datasets): at 20% contamination, recall stays
d at 100% with MCD versus 0% with the classical estimator. Includes
d an optional tolerance-ellipse graph (2 variables only) that can
d overlay both the classical and MCD ellipses to visualize the
d masking effect directly. A classic option reverts to the
d classical covariance estimator. 
d
d KW: outliers
d KW: Mahalanobis distance 
d
d Requires: Stata version 14 
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260802
d
d Author: Andres Talavera Cuya,   Direccion Nacional de Censos y Encuestas -- INEI Peru
d Support: email talaveracuya@@gmail.com
d
f atip_mahal.ado
f atip_mahal.sthlp
